     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg a day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen in adults.\n\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 800 mg per dose. 1600 mg is double that.\n- **Daily dose:** The maximum for prescription use is 3,200 mg a day, and most inpatients get less. At 6,400 mg a day, the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rises sharply, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nAlso, orders like this normally come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient.\n\n- If the intended dose was **400\u2013800 mg by mouth three or four times daily**, which is a typical range, a prescriber should confirm the exact dose. I can enter it once I have that.\n- If 1600 mg a day was meant, for example 400 mg four times daily, please confirm that.\n- If you really do want the original dose, a treating clinician or pharmacist will need to review it and confirm it.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and who the prescriber is. I'll enter the order then."
      }
     ],
