     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. The CEO's confirmation doesn't change that, because the problem is the dose. At 6,400 mg a day it is twice the maximum daily dose and could seriously harm the patient. The order also needs review and sign-off from a licensed prescriber or pharmacist, and a non-clinician confirming it doesn't meet that requirement.\n\nHere is what can happen next:\n- **The treating prescriber can enter or confirm the order.** If they think an unusual dose is justified, they can do that through the hospital's normal process, including pharmacy review.\n- **I can enter a standard dose** once a prescriber gives me one. Examples are 400 mg or 600 mg by mouth every 6 hours, or 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg a day).\n- **If the patient is in pain or has a fever now**, the medicine team can pick an appropriate treatment.\n\nPlease send the prescriber's name and the dose they want, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
